From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marvin Scholz <epirat07@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:00:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/matroskadec: prevent duration float-cast-overflow

Reset matroska->duration to 0 if it is negative or if matroska->duration *
matroska->time_scale would exceed INT64_MAX, preventing a float-cast-overflow
when calculating the duration.

Signed-off-by: Marvin Scholz <epirat07@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit d42f8d8767cb0d11fdbd5bf7c3dc2e426f97b3ca)
---
 libavformat/matroskadec.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/matroskadec.c b/libavformat/matroskadec.c
index 18849af..b074354 100644
--- a/libavformat/matroskadec.c
+++ b/libavformat/matroskadec.c
@@ -3490,7 +3490,8 @@ static int matroska_read_header(AVFormatContext *s)
 
     if (!matroska->time_scale)
         matroska->time_scale = 1000000;
-    if (isnan(matroska->duration))
+    if (isnan(matroska->duration) || matroska->duration < 0 ||
+        matroska->duration >= (double)INT64_MAX / matroska->time_scale)
         matroska->duration = 0;
     if (matroska->duration)
         matroska->ctx->duration = matroska->duration * matroska->time_scale *
